            ('fire', '(of pottery) bake in great heat to harden', 'bake', None, 'The potters ___ the pots in a bonfire of dry wood.'),
            ('brittle', 'hard but easily broken', 'fragile', 'tough', 'Clay that is not fired properly becomes ___.'),
            ('artisan', 'a skilled worker who makes things by hand', 'craftsperson', None, 'The village ___ sold her pots at the weekly market.'),
            ('apprentice', 'a person learning a craft from a skilled worker', 'trainee', 'master', 'Sentila was like an ___ eager to learn the craft.'),
